r1_priorart.md:288:**First experiment:** Implement a transparent block-product baseline, then one recurrence or invariant that attempts to answer only the unit predicate. Compare actual arithmetic counts and largest representation sizes.
r1_priorart.md:290:### Track D — Hidden characteristic, lifted information, and annihilators
r1_priorart.md:310:**First experiment:** Build small lifted or sectioned representations and classify the denominators, pivots, and annihilators that arise. Separate structural factor discovery from accidental divisibility by a small tested integer.
r1_priorart.md:312:### Track E — Transfer partial information into lattices or hidden relations
r1_priorart.md:336:**First experiment:** Specify an exact partial-information format and demonstrate its downstream usefulness with a diagnostic oracle. Then separately attempt to produce it from `N` alone. Never combine those two stages into an unsupported end-to-end speed claim.
r1_priorart.md:338:### Track F — One independent connection
