The exact diagnostics passed after the repair. Among 1,728 quotient probes on 36 independently generated semiprimes, only two had different CRT ranks; both used 8-bit factors. Most factor discoveries came from nonunit matrix entries with equal ranks, which need a matched random-GCD baseline.

I also proved two limits: a binary-section scalar sequence can require exactly \(2^d\) linear states at depth \(d\), and removing the public root from the divided-derivative polynomial eliminates every scalar nonunit when \(\gcd(p-1,q-1)=2\).
